{"t": 1785378038.2, "lenguaje": "html", "temperature": 0.2, "reasoning_effort": null, "max_tokens": null, "system": "You are a creative front-end developer. Write complete, self-contained HTML pages with inline CSS and JavaScript and no external resources. The page must animate by itself on load. Follow the output format exactly.", "prompt": "You are a creative front-end developer making self-contained web pages.\n\nWrite a complete HTML page for: **Un buscaminas 5x5 con 3 minas en posiciones FIJAS en un solo archivo HTML. OBLIGATORIO: 25 celdas <div class=\"c\"> con data-i de 0 a 24; las minas estan en las celdas 6, 12 y 18. Al hacer click en una celda se revela: gana la clase 'abierta' y muestra el numero de minas adyacentes (contando las 8 vecinas), o nada si es 0. REGLA CLAVE: si se abre una celda con 0 minas adyacentes, se abren tambien EN CASCADA todas sus vecinas con 0, y los bordes de esa region. Click derecho pone una bandera (clase 'bandera') y una celda con bandera NO se abre al hacer click. <div id=\"estado\"> dice 'perdiste' si se abre una mina.. TARGET LOOK, match it: A compact 5×5 grid of square tiles, each a crisp 64×64px button with a subtle raised shadow. The top region shows a simple score counter and a reset icon; the bottom holds a single “Play Again” button. Tile colors shift from light gray (closed) to soft sky-blue (open with 0 adjacent mines), to a gradient of pastel blues and greens for numbers 1–8, with a bright crimson for the 3 fixed mines. Typography is a clean sans‑serif (e.g., Montserrat) in 18px, centered numbers in tiles, and bold 24px for the counter. The hierarchy guides the eye from the counter to the grid to the reset button, creating a calm, approachable Minesweeper experience.**\n\nCRITICAL RULES — all must be followed:\n- ONE single self-contained .html file\n- Inline <style> and <script> — no external files\n- NO external resources: no CDN, no <link href=http...>, no fetch(), no remote images or fonts. It must work fully offline.\n- Implement EXACTLY the behavior the idea specifies. Nothing happens on its own: NO setInterval animations and NO random data unless the idea explicitly asks for them.\n- The INITIAL state must match the idea exactly (e.g. a counter that starts at 0 shows 0 and only changes on user action).\n- Reproduce LITERALLY every id=, class= and element the idea marks as required: automated tests will query those exact selectors.\n- Draw charts as inline <svg> — NOT <canvas>, and never a chart library\n- Responsive and legible on a phone screen\n- If you color-code state (up/down, green/red), put the state class on the SAME element your CSS selector targets. A rule like `.row.up span` only works if the class lands on `.row`, not on the inner span.\n- Set colors with a rule that matches the element you actually modify, and prefer setting style/class on the element you create in JS\n- Write ALL visible text in the SAME language as the page topic above\n- If you use <canvas>: set canvas.width = canvas.clientWidth and canvas.height = canvas.clientHeight BEFORE drawing, and redraw on resize. A canvas stretched by CSS from its default 300x150 renders squashed and blurry. Inline <svg> avoids this entirely and is preferred\n- Format numbers for humans: thousands separators, 2 decimals, currency symbol where money (toLocaleString)\n- Render a complete first frame IMMEDIATELY on load — never a blank page waiting for the first setInterval tick\n- REQUIRED component 1: Un buscaminas 5x5 con 3 minas en posiciones FIJAS en un solo archivo HTML. OBLIGATORIO: 25 celdas <div class=\"c\"> con data-i de 0 a 24; las minas estan en las celdas 6\n- REQUIRED component 2: 12 y 18. Al hacer click en una celda se revela: gana la clase 'abierta'\n- REQUIRED component 3: muestra el numero de minas adyacentes (contando las 8 vecinas)\n- REQUIRED component 4: o nada si es 0. REGLA CLAVE: si se abre una celda con 0 minas adyacentes\n- REQUIRED component 5: se abren tambien EN CASCADA todas sus vecinas con 0\n- REQUIRED component 6: los bordes de esa region. Click derecho pone una bandera (clase 'bandera')\n- REQUIRED component 7: una celda con bandera NO se abre al hacer click. <div id=\"estado\"> dice 'perdiste' si se abre una mina.. TARGET LOOK\n- REQUIRED component 8: match it: A compact 5×5 grid of square tiles\n- REQUIRED component 9: each a crisp 64×64px button with a subtle raised shadow. The top region shows a simple score counter and a reset icon; the bottom holds a single “Play Again” button. Tile colors shift from light gray (closed) to soft sky-blue (open with 0 adjacent mines)\n- REQUIRED component 10: to a gradient of pastel blues and greens for numbers 1–8\n- Implement EVERY required component above — a page that skips any of them is WRONG. Prefer a LONGER page over an incomplete one; there is no size limit.\n- Demonstrate itself with built-in sample data and print results.\n\nPROVEN PATTERNS from pages that already passed browser checks and professional review. ADAPT their techniques to this idea — do NOT copy them verbatim; change data, labels, colors and layout to fit:\n--- grafico_svg ---\n<!-- PATRON: grafico de linea SVG con ejes y escala segura.\n     Por que funciona: <text> en el eje Y (sin etiquetas no se sabe que\n     numeros muestra); la escala se calcula de los datos con RANGO MINIMO\n     (sin el, min==max en el primer tick da division por cero y los\n     atributos salen NaN — error real medido); rejilla fina y recesiva. -->\n<svg id=\"grafico\" width=\"100%\" height=\"220\" viewBox=\"0 0 600 220\"></svg>\n<script>\nfunction pintar(datos) {                       // datos: [num, num, ...]\n  var svg = document.getElementById('grafico');\n  var M = {arriba: 12, abajo: 22, izq: 56, der: 12}, W = 600, H = 220;\n  var y0 = Math.min.apply(null, datos), y1 = Math.max.apply(null, datos);\n  if (y1 - y0 < 1) { y0 -= 1; y1 += 1; }       // <- la proteccion anti-NaN\n  var x = function(i){ return M.izq + (W-M.izq-M.der) * i / Math.max(1, datos.length-1); };\n  var y = function(v){ return M.arriba + (H-M.arriba-M.abajo) * (1 - (v-y0)/(y1-y0)); };\n  var linea = datos.map(function(v,i){ return (i?'L':'M') + x(i).toFixed(1) + ',' + y(v).toFixed(1); }).join('');\n  var rejilla = '', etiquetas = '';\n  for (var k = 0; k <= 3; k++) {\n    var v = y0 + (y1-y0) * k/3, yy = y(v).toFixed(1);\n    rejilla += '<line x1=\"'+M.izq+'\" x2=\"'+(W-M.der)+'\" y1=\"'+yy+'\" y2=\"'+yy+'\" stroke=\"#e1e0d9\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>';\n    etiquetas += '<text x=\"'+(M.izq-8)+'\" y=\"'+yy+'\" dy=\"4\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#898781\">'+Math.round(v).toLocaleString('es-ES')+'</text>';\n  }\n  svg.innerHTML = rejilla + etiquetas +\n    '<path d=\"'+linea+'\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a78d6\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/>';\n}\n</script>\n\n--- tabla_estados ---\n<!-- PATRON: tabla de valores con estados pintados sobre los valores VIVOS.\n     Por que funciona: el color va por estilo inline en el MISMO elemento\n     cuyo textContent cambia (no depende de que un selector CSS case);\n     flecha + color, nunca color solo; tabular-nums alinea las columnas. -->\n<table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px\">\n  <thead><tr>\n    <th style=\"text-align:left;color:#898781;font-size:12px\">Valor</th>\n    <th style=\"text-align:right;color:#898781;font-size:12px\">Precio</th>\n    <th style=\"text-align:right;color:#898781;font-size:12px\">Cambio</th>\n  </tr></thead>\n  <tbody id=\"posiciones\"></tbody>\n</table>\n<script>\nfunction fila(sim, precio, cambio) {\n  var tr = document.createElement('tr');\n  var color = cambio >= 0 ? '#006300' : '#d03b3b';\n  var flecha = cambio >= 0 ? '▲' : '▼';\n  tr.innerHTML =\n    '<td><strong>' + sim + '</strong></td>' +\n    '<td style=\"text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums\">' +\n      precio.toLocaleString('es-ES', {style:'currency',currency:'EUR'}) + '</td>' +\n    '<td style=\"text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;color:' + color + '\">' +\n      flecha + ' ' + Math.abs(cambio).toFixed(2) + '</td>';\n  return tr;\n}\n</script>\n\n\nRespond EXACTLY in this format:\n\nTitle: <short title>\nDescription: <one sentence>\nHTML Code:\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<complete working page>\n```"}
